{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"51858d802f9ef6e2","name":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Base/units/card_unit_j1n1_gekko","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"J1N1 GEKKO","text":"Your orders deal +1 damage.","flavorText":"The Nakajima J1N1 Gekko was a Japanese twin-engine aircraft used by the Japanese Imperial Navy during WWII as a night combat, reconnaissance aircraft and lastly for kamikaze missions. It was first introduced in 1942, first for reconnaissance and later as a night fighter. The night fighter variant had a twin 20 mm Type 99 Model 1 cannon firing upward in a 30° upward angle, and a second pair firing downward at a forward 30° angle, allowing attacks from above or below. This arrangement was effective against the Allied B-17 Flying Fortress Bombers and B-24 Liberators. By the end of the war a number of Gekko's were used for Kamikaze attacks where they had 250 kg bombs attached to the wings.","faction":"Japan","type":"fighter","rarity":"Common","cost":5,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"Name":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko_title","SourceString":"J1N1 GEKKO","LocalizedString":"J1N1 GEKKO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":3,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko_text","SourceString":"Your orders deal +1 damage.","LocalizedString":"Your orders deal +1 damage."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko_history","SourceString":"The Nakajima J1N1 Gekko was a Japanese twin-engine aircraft used by the Japanese Imperial Navy during WWII as a night combat, reconnaissance aircraft and lastly for kamikaze missions. It was first introduced in 1942, first for reconnaissance and later as a night fighter. The night fighter variant had a twin 20 mm Type 99 Model 1 cannon firing upward in a 30° upward angle, and a second pair firing downward at a forward 30° angle, allowing attacks from above or below. This arrangement was effective against the Allied B-17 Flying Fortress Bombers and B-24 Liberators. By the end of the war a number of Gekko's were used for Kamikaze attacks where they had 250 kg bombs attached to the wings.","LocalizedString":"The Nakajima J1N1 Gekko was a Japanese twin-engine aircraft used by the Japanese Imperial Navy during WWII as a night combat, reconnaissance aircraft and lastly for kamikaze missions. It was first introduced in 1942, first for reconnaissance and later as a night fighter. The night fighter variant had a twin 20 mm Type 99 Model 1 cannon firing upward in a 30° upward angle, and a second pair firing downward at a forward 30° angle, allowing attacks from above or below. This arrangement was effective against the Allied B-17 Flying Fortress Bombers and B-24 Liberators. By the end of the war a number of Gekko's were used for Kamikaze attacks where they had 250 kg bombs attached to the wings."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamageAddDamage"],"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_j1n1_gekko.t_j1n1_gekko","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Darryl Legg","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/J1N1_GEKKO.J1N1_GEKKO","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":226.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Wikimedia","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko_photo","SourceString":"J1N1 Gekko at rest, 1940s.","LocalizedString":"J1N1 Gekko at rest, 1940s."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_j1n1_gekko_header",